    "title": "pandas.Series.keys — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.keys#\n\n- Series.keys()[source]#\n- Return alias for index. This method provides dictionary-like compatibility by returning the index of the Series, analogous to the keys of a dictionary. \n  - Returns:\n    - Index\n    - Index of the Series.\n See also \n  - `Series.index`\n  - The index (axis labels) of the Series.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3], index=[0, 1, 2]) >>> s.keys() Index([0, 1, 2], dtype='int64')",
